  "neighborhood_description": "\u6b4c\u821e\u4f0e\u753a\u4e00\u4e01\u76eeis Tokyo's most notorious entertainment district, radiating outward from JR\u65b0\u5bbf\u99c5's east exit along 2\u756a\u901a\u308a and 3\u756a\u901a\u308a into a labyrinth of host clubs, izakayas, pachinko parlors, and love hotels. The area operates almost entirely at night\u2014neon-lit storefronts in Japanese, Chinese, and Thai crowd every block, while \u30ed\u30fc\u30bd\u30f3 and \u30bb\u30d6\u30f3-\u30a4\u30ec\u30d6\u30f3 serve as the only real community anchors. Newcomers should orient by TOHO\u30b7\u30cd\u30de\u30ba to the north and \u30bf\u30a4\u30c8\u30fc\u30b9\u30c6\u30fc\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3 near the main drag; \u67cf\u6728\u516c\u5712 offers the sole green respite to the west. Anonymity is a civic virtue here\u2014nobody asks why you moved, and nobody expects you to stay.",
